@startuml fig-22-withdrawal-activity
' =====================================================================
' Figure 22. Withdrawing: four routes out, and what happens to your data on each
' Type            : PlantUML-type, activity diagram with swimlanes
' Paper section   : § 8, Stopping, Withdrawing, Changing Your Mind
' Concern answered: ChatGPT concern 10 (privacy, recording, and secondary data
'                   use) and concern 16 (post-trial burdens); Gemini family 4.
'                   Patients are routinely told they may withdraw at any time
'                   and are almost never told what withdrawal does to the data
'                   already collected. The honest answer is that it depends on
'                   which route out is taken, and there are four. This figure
'                   draws all four and their data consequences side by side.
' Why this type   : Swimlanes assign responsibility for each action, and an
'                   activity diagram carries decision nodes, fork and join, and
'                   terminal nodes in one notation. Nothing else shows both
'                   "who does this" and "what happens to the record" at once.
'
' TikZ: draw with the uml* vocabulary of patientstyle.sty.
' TikZ: Three vertical swimlanes as umlpkg rectangles, x centres at
' TikZ:   -5.0, 0.6, 6.6, widths 4.4cm, 5.0cm, 4.8cm, each titled at the top in
' TikZ:   umlpkgtab; lanes share one top and one bottom edge.
' TikZ: Actions are umlstate rounded boxes, text width 26mm, stacked with 2.2cm
' TikZ:   pitch so at least 9mm of clear space separates ranks.
' TikZ: The single decision is an mmdec diamond at (0.6,-3.0), text width 24mm.
' TikZ: The fork and the join are umlbar filled rectangles 26mm wide, 1.2mm
' TikZ:   tall, at y = -6.0 and y = -12.4.
' TikZ: Four terminal nodes are umlfinal ringed discs on one rank at y = -14.2.
' TikZ: Cross-lane edges leave a lane at its boundary and enter the next at the
' TikZ:   same y, using -| right-angle routing; the two that must change rank
' TikZ:   use to[out=0,in=180,looseness=0.85].
' TikZ: Data-consequence notes are umlnote boxes anchored to the right of their
' TikZ:   branch, connected by a 0.5pt dashed leader, never overlapping a box.
' =====================================================================

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #6C757D
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #00417A
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #CED4DA
skinparam ActivityBarColor #000000
skinparam ActivityStartColor #00417A
skinparam ActivityEndColor #00417A
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #6C757D
skinparam SwimlaneTitleBackgroundColor #DCE8F1
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E9ECEF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #6C757D

|#FFFFFF|You|
start
:Decide to stop;
note right #E9ECEF
  No reason is required at any
  point below, and none is
  recorded unless you give one.
end note
:Tell any member of the study
team, in any form, at any visit;

|#FFFFFF|Site study team|
:Log the request with a timestamp
in the hash-chained record;
if (Which route out?) then (A: stop the drug only)
  |You|
  :Daraxonrasib discontinued;
  |Site study team|
  :Surgery, follow-up visits,
  and safety reporting continue;
  |#FFFFFF|Data and specimens|
  :Everything already collected stays
  in the safety analysis. New data
  continues to be collected;
  stop
elseif (B: stop study procedures,
keep follow-up) then
  |You|
  :No further study procedures;
  |Site study team|
  :Follow-up contact continues by
  telephone or record review only;
  |Data and specimens|
  :Existing data retained. New data
  limited to survival status.
  Specimens retained unless you
  ask for destruction;
  stop
elseif (C: full withdrawal) then
  |You|
  :All study participation ends;
  |Site study team|
  :Standard-of-care oncology
  continues, unchanged and
  without penalty;
  |Data and specimens|
  :Data already collected cannot be
  removed from the safety analysis,
  because removing it would bias the
  record for everyone else. Nothing
  new is collected. Specimens
  destroyed on request;
  stop
else (D: withdraw consent for
data use as well)
  |You|
  :Participation and future data
  use both end;
  |Site study team|
  :Request forwarded to the IRB
  and recorded in the audit chain;
  |Data and specimens|
  :Identifiable data segregated and
  no longer used for any new
  analysis. Aggregate safety data
  already reported to the FDA
  cannot be recalled;
  stop
endif

@enduml
